  "chapter": {
    "number": 79,
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "hebrew_subtitle",
        "content": [
          "(80) For the",
          {
            "noteId": 146
          },
          "end, for alternate strains, a testimony for Asaph, a Psalm concerning the Assyrian."
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 1,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Attend, O Shepherd of Israel, who guide Joseph like a flock; you who sit upon the cherubs, manifest yourself;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 2,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "before Ephraim and Benjamin and Manasse, stir up your power, and come to deliver us.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 3,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Turn us, O God, and cause your face to shine; and we shall be delivered.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 4,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O Lord God of hosts, how long are you angry with the prayer of your servant?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 5,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You will feed us with bread of tears; and will cause us to drink tears by measure.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 6,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have made us a strife to our neighbors; and our enemies have mocked at us.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 7,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Turn us, O Lord God of hosts, and cause your face to shine; and we shall be saved. Pause.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 8,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You have transplanted a vine out of Egypt: you have cast out the heathen, and planted it.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 9,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "You made a way before it, and did cause its roots to strike, and the land was filled with it.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 10,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Its shadow covered the mountains, and its shoots equalled the",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 147
          },
          {
            "text": "goodly cedars.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 11,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "It sent forth its branches to the sea, and its shoots to the river.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 12,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Therefore have you broken down its hedge, while all that pass by the way pluck it?",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 13,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "The boar out of the wood has laid it waste, and the wild beast has devoured it.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 14,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "O God of hosts, turn, we pray you: look on us from heaven, and behold and visit this vine;",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 15,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "and restore that which your right hand has planted: and look on the son of man whom you did strengthen for yourself.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 16,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "It is burnt with fire and dug up: they shall perish at the rebuke of your",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "noteId": 148
          },
          {
            "text": "presence.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 17,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Let your hand be upon the man of your right hand, and upon the son of man whom you did strengthen for yourself.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 18,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "So will we not depart from you: you shall quicken us, and we will call upon your name.",
            "poem": 1
          },
          {
            "lineBreak": true
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "verse",
        "number": 19,
        "content": [
          {
            "text": "Turn us, O Lord God of hosts, and make your face to shine; and we shall be saved.",
            "poem": 1
          }
        ]
      }
    ],
